# `data/` is both a source package (the vendor adapters) and, historically, a
# runtime scratch directory. Ignore its contents by default and re-include the
# source that lives there: without this, new modules under data/ are silently
# untracked (the existing ones predate the rule and are tracked already).
/data/*
!/data/*.py
!/data/prices/
sessions/
/sessions/
cache/
caches/
.Codex/
